INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Issues 1 & 2: RequestMetricsController NullPointerException
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Problem**: The `RequestMetricsController.init()` method was throwing a `NullPointerException` at line 100 when `metricsRegistry.meter()` returned null or when `metricsRegistry` itself was null during test context initialization.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Solution**: Added null checks in three methods:
INFO  [Claude Code] - `init()` method - checks if `metricsRegistry` is null before initializing metrics
INFO  [Claude Code] - `initStatusCode()` method - checks if `metricsRegistry` or the returned `meter` is null before proceeding
INFO  [Claude Code] - `initController()` method - checks if `metricsRegistry` or `requestsTimer` is null before initializing integration-specific metrics
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] These changes allow the bean to initialize gracefully even when dependencies are mocked or not fully configured in test contexts.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **File modified**: `integration-web/src/main/java/org/symphonyoss/integration/web/metrics/RequestMetricsController.java`
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Issue 3: WebHookResource bean ambiguity
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Problem**: Spring was unable to register a mock bean for `WebHookResource` because it found two beans of that type: `webHookDispatcherResource` and `webHookResource`. The abstract `WebHookResource` class was annotated with `@RestController`, causing Spring to create a bean instance for an abstract class.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Solution**: Removed the `@RestController` annotation from the abstract `WebHookResource` class while keeping the `@RequestMapping("/v1/whi")` annotation. This prevents Spring from creating a bean for the abstract class while still allowing the concrete subclasses (`WebHookDispatcherResource` and `WebHookWelcomeResource`) to inherit the base path mapping.
